---
// One-off illustration for this case study, not a design system component.
import styles from "./token-diagram.module.css";
import SectionHeader from "@molecules/section-header/section-header.astro";

interface Props {
  id: string;
  index?: string;
}

const { id, index } = Astro.props;
const headingId = `${id}-heading`;

// Illustrative names: replace with real examples from the Nurun system.
const layers = [
  {
    name: "Primitive tokens",
    note: "Raw values",
    examples: ["color-blue-600: #1F5FBF", "space-16: 16px"],
    description: "The raw values, such as colors and spacing.",
  },
  {
    name: "Semantic tokens",
    note: "Themes swap here",
    examples: ["color-action-primary", "space-component-padding"],
    description: "Give those values meaning and intent. This is the layer each brand theme replaces.",
  },
  {
    name: "Utility classes",
    note: "Built on tokens",
    examples: [".bg-action-primary", ".p-component"],
    description: "Consistent styling without one-off values.",
  },
];
---

<section id={id} class={styles["nc-token-diagram"]} aria-labelledby={headingId}>
  <SectionHeader id={headingId} title="Token architecture" index={index} />
  <p class={styles["nc-token-diagram__text"]}>
    With the project’s UI lead and another designer, I defined a token foundation designed to scale and to enable theming, in three layers:
  </p>
  <ol class={styles["nc-token-diagram__layers"]}>
    {layers.map((layer, layerIndex) => (
      <li class={styles["nc-token-diagram__layer"]}>
        <p class={styles["nc-token-diagram__note"]}>
          <span aria-hidden="true">{String(layerIndex + 1).padStart(2, "0")}</span>
          {layer.note}
        </p>
        <h3 class={styles["nc-token-diagram__name"]}>{layer.name}</h3>
        <ul class={styles["nc-token-diagram__examples"]}>
          {layer.examples.map((example) => <li><code>{example}</code></li>)}
        </ul>
        <p class={styles["nc-token-diagram__description"]}>{layer.description}</p>
      </li>
    ))}
  </ol>
  <p class={styles["nc-token-diagram__text"]}>
    Replacing the old list of CSS variables would have meant more refactoring than the budget allowed, so the new tokens were added as a separate system, living in parallel with the old variables. Theming was rolled out to every brand: new development used it fully, while existing styles were only partly migrated.
  </p>
</section>